   153	
   154	`edges i~j iff j-i belongs to +/-D`,
   155	
   156	`D is any subset of {1,2,3,4,5}`.
   157	
   158	For each graph, generate every Pauli of weights one, two, and three: `33+495+4455=4983` errors. Translate a prospective word set to contain 0. Define V to be every nonzero word that is neither an induced nonzero error nor forbidden by a zero-syndrome phase constraint. Two vertices a,b in V are adjacent exactly when their difference is not an induced nonzero error. The phase constraints are linear, so the difference automatically satisfies them.
   159	
