the number of coordinates E acts non-trivially on. The Knill-Laflamme conditions then
give a complete characterization of quantum error-correcting codes [KL97]: Let Π be a
projector onto a code subspace of rank K acting on (C2 )⊗n . The code Π has distance δ,
if and only if for all E ∈ En with 0 ≤ wt(E) < δ,
